.TH objectinfo n 2.0 Tclpp "Tclpp Built-In Commands"
.BS
.SH NAME
objectinfo \- Obtain information about objects (instances)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBobjectinfo\fR \fIobject\fR \fIoption\fR ?\fIarg ...\fR?
.SH DESCRIPTION
This command provides information about objects. The legal options (which may 
be abbreviated) are:
.TP
\fBobjectinfo\fR \fIobject\fR \fBisA\fR
Returns the fully qualified class name (starting with \fB::\fR) of
the \fIobject\fR.
.TP
\fBobjectinfo\fR \fIobject\fR \fBisKindOf\fR \fIclass\fR
Returns \fI1\fR if the \fIobject\fR is (derived from) \fIclass\fR.
Returns \fI0\fR otherwise.
.LP

.SH AUTHOR(S)
Stefan Sinnige (ssinnige@geocities.com)
.SH SEE ALSO
class(n), classinfo(n)
